Upstream libuv is MIT licensed; LICENSE-extra retains its additional notices.
The Pyxis platform selection patch retains upstream MIT terms.
Original native adapter, recipe and documentation are MPL-2.0 under the ports
repository LICENSE. The adapter uses native capabilities and libc descriptors;
it does not compile the upstream Unix or Windows backends or worker pool.

The native os.c supplies uv_os_uname and uv_os_gethostname from SYSTEM_INFO
READ, and uv_os_homedir/uv_os_tmpdir from the caller's home/tmp roots. Without
SYSTEM_INFO, uname retains Pyxis/x86_64 and empty release/version fields;
hostname returns UV_EACCES. Missing directory roots return UV_ENOENT. Passwd,
group and priority queries remain unsupported rather than inventing values.
